    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d301">

                <pb facs="0362" n="1096" xml:id="pg1096"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Breckinridge to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August 29, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Sept. 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 135.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 130, in regard to John
                    Ginzberg, I now have to say that I am informed by a note from Mr. Chichkine that
                    the foreign office has been informed by the ministry of justice that the
                    necessary steps have been taken to hasten the progress of his case.</p>
                <p>The appeal to the minister of the interior to dismiss the case is still
                    pending.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clifton R. Breckinridge.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
